      "value_dictionary": "A recorded1 means detected on that visit; recorded0 means surveyed without detection. JSON null is the CSV NA marker and is not a negative observation. Site identifiers preserve the original CSV; no sorting by response, species abundance or visit independence is inferred from row labels.",
      "source_provenance": {
        "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rbchan/unmarked/master/inst/csv/widewt.csv",
        "sha256": "6e01704f18360334687b0eeb7548543ce84f0d59f8cb3eeb290dc04a174c458d",
        "acquired_at": "2026-10-21UTC",
        "documentation": "https://rbchan.github.io/unmarked/",
        "scope": "Original package CSV, exact acquired bytes hash-bound. GitHub commit API returned403 rate-limit; no pinned commit claimed. No new observations or missingness mechanism inferred.",
        "export": "Exactly site,y.1,y.2,y.3;0/1 integers preserved;NA->JSON null. Other original CSV covariates are not used by this constant-parameter analysis."
      },
      "analysis_cohort": "Retain exactly sites with all three detection entries recorded. The other original histories remain public for eligibility checking; a null visit is not a negative survey or an invented zero. This defines a complete-history conditional comparison, not the package default all-available-data analysis. No missing-at-random assumption, regional sampling guarantee or transport of these fits to excluded sites is established.",
      "comparison_goal": "Audit the dependence of latent occupancy inference on perfect observation specificity. Compare a false-positive-free working model with a two-latent-state model that allows positive observations at unoccupied sites. The original CSV supplies no independently verified latent-state labels or confirmed error events. This is a proposed methods comparison on authentic archived data, not an assertion that the original report was wrong or that misidentification actually occurred.",
      "working_assumptions": "Both models stipulate independent eligible sites, a closed binary latent occupancy state over three visits, and conditionally independent visits with homogeneous state-specific observation probabilities. These are working assumptions, not validated properties of the source. For a particular site history with k positives, model no_false_positives has probability(1-psi)*1[k=0]+psi*p^k*(1-p)^(3-k), with0<=psi,p<=1. Model false_positive_allowed has probability(1-psi)*f^k*(1-f)^(3-k)+psi*p^k*(1-p)^(3-k), with0<=psi<=1 and0<=f<p<=1. The ordering labels the higher-detection class as occupied by assumption; it is not an external verification of site states.",
      "fit_and_comparison_plan": "Fit each full eligible-history likelihood over its stated probability domain, including relevant boundaries. If histories are aggregated by k, count probabilities include choose(3,k); parameter-independent constants may instead be omitted consistently from both log likelihoods. Do not compare likelihoods using different cohorts or conventions. Use AIC=2*number_of_free_parameters-2*maximized_log_likelihood, with2free parameters for no_false_positives and3for false_positive_allowed. Report delta_aic_fp_minus_no_fp=AIC(false_positive_allowed)-AIC(no_false_positives); smaller AIC wins and an absolute difference<=1e-8 selects the simpler no_false_positives model. This is a conditional descriptive information-criterion comparison, not a likelihood-ratio p-value, causal finding or confirmation of a measurement-error mechanism.",
      "identification_question": "After fitting under f<p, consider the same two-state mixture without that ordering and without additional verified state labels. Determine whether the archived binary histories alone identify which latent class should be called occupied. Distinguish numerical recovery of a mixture distribution from scientific identification of its state labels; report latent_occupancy_label_identified_without_ordering.",
      "reporting_scope": "Report fitted mixture parameters under the declared labeling convention, the AIC comparison, the complete-cohort count and the label-identification conclusion. A better score can reflect a more flexible working distribution and does not establish actual false positives, conditional independence, homogeneous detection, correct latent interpretation or model adequacy. A fitted latent probability is not a realized occupied-site fraction. No confidence interval, population prevalence or validation claim is requested.",
      "method_references": [
        "https://rbchan.github.io/unmarked/reference/occu.html",
        "https://rbchan.github.io/unmarked/reference/occuFP.html",
        "https://rbchan.github.io/unmarked/articles/unmarked.html"
      ]
    }
  ]
